# Cinematic Portfolio Project Rules

## 1. Core Tech Stack & UI Framework
- **Framework:** Next.js (App Router) with TypeScript, optimized for high performance and smooth server/client component separation.
- **UI & Styling:** Tailwind CSS combined with **shadcn/ui** components for accessible, modern primitive design.
- **Performance & Structure:** Keep 3D canvas and heavy animation logic modular so the app maintains a buttery-smooth 60+ FPS user experience.

## 2. Animation & 3D Engineering (GSAP & Three.js)
- **Three.js / React Three Fiber (R3F):** Used for immersive, performant 3D hero sections or background elements. Manage canvas rendering efficiently to prevent memory leaks.
- **GSAP (GreenSock):** Use for precise timeline-based UI transitions, scroll-driven animations (`ScrollTrigger`), and fluid micro-interactions.
- **Clean Animation Architecture:** Separate animation logic from core component markup using custom hooks or clean ref handling (`useRef`) so code remains readable.

## 3. Interview-Ready Code & Explanation Standards
- **Walkthrough-Friendly:** Every complex animation controller, Three.js scene setup, or state transition must feature clear, educational inline comments. 
- **Self-Documenting Logic:** Write clean variable names and architectural patterns that you can confidently project, highlight, and explain line-by-line during a live technical or portfolio walkthrough interview.